WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.400
Kunugigaoka School of Magic,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.330
where they teach students how to be heroes.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.740
But the E Class alone shared a special secret
the other classes didn't know:

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.170
The teacher instructing us...

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.160
...was the Big Bad!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.870
Now, let's get to our schoolwork!

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.250
Another day with Koro Sensei,
another truly unusual adventure!

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.980
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.400
"Nagisa"

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.070
"Karma"

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.070
"Kaede"

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.410
"Isogai" "Maehara"

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.080
"Rio" "Okuda" "Sugino" "Kanzaki"

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.580
"Chiba" "Hayami"

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:04.080
"Hinata" "Meg"

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.580
"Hinano" "Takebayashi" "Toka" "Justice"

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:08.580
"Muramatsu" "Kirara" "Yoshida" "Terasaka"

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:10.590
"Okajima" "Hara" "Mimura" "Fuwa" "Sugaya"

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.590
"Karasuma" "Irina"

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.900
"The Red Devil"

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.780
Now, my goal is to train up a party
that can fight the Big Bad on his level.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.990
And to do that...

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.490
...we'll need some heroes.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:43.080
"Hero"

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.080
But right now, no one in this class
has what it takes to be that hero.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.040
What about Isogai?

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.860
True, Isogai has the leadership skills
to command a party.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.030
He's probably the closest thing to a hero here.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.130
However...

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.010
When seen from behind, Isogai is also
the <i>furthest</i> thing from a hero!

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.470
Oh, right!

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:01.180
If Isogai's no good...
don't we have anyone else that's hero-y?

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.220
If I may be so bold as to suggest yours truly?

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.020
The Big Bad is <i>the</i> furthest from a hero!

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.850
So what can we do?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:16.820
"Royal Knight Commander" "Karasuma"

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.980
Rumors of powerful warriors on this continent

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.110
always mention the same three people.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.400
Commander Karasuma!
Where'd you come from?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.610
You must entice one of the three to join you.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.700
The first is Karma, the Red Devil,
said to live in a northern cave.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.700
The abilities of this young genius
are reputedly all above average.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.830
I've heard of <i>him</i>!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.670
They say he's a super-sadistic ranger!

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.840
To think someone that famous
was living so nearby...

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.960
The second is Ritsu, the Evolved Mage.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.220
She lives in a cave to the north,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.760
and her magic is said
to evolve on a daily basis.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.720
And finally, the Silver Berserker, Itona.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.600
--He's rumored to live
in a cave up north, where--

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.060
--Just how many caves do they <i>have</i> up there?!
--He's rumored to live
in a cave up north, where--

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.690
Koro-Q!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.690
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.150
"Ace Sorceress: Confessing the Truth"

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.230
Say it! Come on! Spill your secret!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.740
That New Year's money
you asked Mom to hold on to?

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.280
You're not going to get it back!

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.240
No way!

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.200
Koro-Q!

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.200
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.910
Here's the cave where the Red Devil lives:

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.450
Karma's Cave.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.210
That's the name of the dungeon?!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.500
"Karma's Cave"

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:14.000
Okay, please hand these out--one apiece.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.670
What <i>is</i> this? It's so heavy!

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.590
The strategy guide for this dungeon.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.720
Monsters, directions, treasure chests--

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.840
even recovery points,
all researched and collected by me!

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.720
It's Koro Sensei's strategy guide! No sweat!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.720
"Karma's Cave: Complete Strategy Guide"
"No sweat: It's Koro Sensei's strategy guide."

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.480
I just get so excited
being on the attacking side!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.850
<i>Too</i> excited.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.440
The book has a sealed-up section
with some slightly smutty monster info.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.190
We're gonna see slightly smutty monsters?!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:44.780
And the last page has info
on the dungeon boss, natch.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:48.990
"Karma (Boss)" "The final boss of
Karma's Cave. Fearless and mischievous."
"Parameters: Excellent in all areas. Battle prowess is especially high." "Irregularities in his Luck Trait"

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.660
"Irregularities in his Luck trait"?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.370
What's that mean?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.170
Hmph. All bark and no bite, eh?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.340
I doubt you'll ever have a hope
of defeating me as long as you live.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.300
When he belittles people
and makes fun of his opponents...

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.220
What are you lousy mutts laughing at?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:10.310
Why don't you just run on back
to your doghouses?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.640
If he keeps up with the disdain and contempt...

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.730
<i>His</i> bug drops his Luck to a negative value

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.110
the second he belittles
or makes fun of someone.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.610
"Luck: -258"

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.610
He's buggy?!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.490
He'd be a top warrior without that habit
of treating others with contempt.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.040
Once he's in the party,
I'll take plenty good care of him!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.660
But that's your face
for treating <i>us</i> with contempt!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.710
The place sure is packed with dangerous traps.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.300
He's even more sadistic than the rumors say.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.510
Not that they'll have the slightest effect
against Koro Sensei, though.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.430
A little dab of poison
ought to up the danger quotient.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.600
He's touching up the traps!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.190
I bet painting something
eye-catching on these axes

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.730
could make them a lot more dangerous!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.770
That's dangerous in a whole 'nother way!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.700
With Koro Sensei handling
trap after trap for us,

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.700
it's pretty easy to make our way through.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.570
Then there are the monsters...

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:10.160
There's one! A monster!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.870
Is it a smutty one?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.370
Nope. Damn.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.830
"Some Mushroom Kunudons draw near!"

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.290
They're in the strategy guide:

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.630
"When they see adventurers at lower levels
than themselves, they smirk."

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.220
--That's a smirk!
--What an obnoxious monster!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.350
Just like bugs flying into the flame!

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.300
Tee-hee-hee-hee...

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.970
The cave is crawling with 'em!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.350
Are we going to be okay?

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.520
Monsters can't attack the Big Bad,
so <i>I</i> will be just fine!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.060
No fair!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.740
Karma!

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.200
Going undercover as a monster?!

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.700
He's the first!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.200
The first we've seen do damage to Koro Sensei!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:56.750
I've heard about you: the Big Bad,
taking on a schoolteacher gig.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.630
I heard they call you "Koro Sensei"
because you're unkillable.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.550
But to be caught by such a simple move?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:06.090
--Too close.
--What's this? Are you a pushover after all?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.760
--Too close.
--What's this? Are you a pushover after all?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.260
Your face is <i>too close</i>!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.470
"Karma looked down on the Big Bad!"

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.020
"Karma fell through a trap door!"

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.350
Karma!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.020
That bug's a doozy!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.430
What awful luck!

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.480
But he <i>did</i> land the first blow on Koro Sensei.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.690
His skills live up to the hype.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.150
Go bald.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.950
--What's he been doing all this time?
Punching the wall?
--Lose your hair. You're a man among men, but go bald.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.530
--All that smack-talking
must have made him mad.
--Lose your hair. You're a man among men, but go bald.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.830
Oh, how careless of me.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:37.410
For a Big Bad, you're a real lightweight.
Guess I let my guard down.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.620
Ah, if it isn't Nagisa!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.330
It's been a while.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.250
Y-Yeah, sure has.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.460
You know each other?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.420
Uh-huh. We grew up together.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.140
What business do you have
tagging along with the Big Bad, Nagisa?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.720
He's belittling Nagisa!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.640
--And you!
--The truth is...

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.760
"And you"

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.390
...we want you to join our party!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.980
So we can beat the Big Bad!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.900
Seeing your attack earlier
reminded me how amazing you are.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.190
Do you think you could
maybe lend that power to us?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.650
Huh...

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.820
He's totally looking down on us.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:14.240
But even if I <i>don't</i> join up with you all...

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.110
Like, <i>way</i> down on us!

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.960
"Trap"

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.960
...I could still do it--all by myself.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.920
Go ba-aaagh!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:23.670
Gotcha!

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.800
Why me?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.590
Where'd he go?

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.510
You're too slow--
and now I'm all nice and clean!

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.680
Fresh out of a bath?!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:40.310
It was so dull being in your trap
that I swapped in a substitute,

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.810
zoomed off to a recovery spring,
and had myself a little soak.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.900
Healed that wound right up, too.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.780
You don't wash yourself in a recovery spring!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.910
--Dammit!
--Pshew!

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:53.960
Hah!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.240
In you go!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:03.670
"Koroseptic"

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.160
You're strong, Karma.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.670
And smart, and quick-witted to boot.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.380
Where do you get off
washing someone else's back?!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.300
I'm gonna shake him.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:15.590
"No running in the bath, kids!"

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.280
But you put too much confidence
in your own abilities.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.590
Your blade can never reach me like that.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.390
Isn't the Big Bad not for
one person to defeat alone,

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.680
but for a whole hero-led party
to defeat together?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.150
Your attack with the monster stand-in
was a very good one.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:31.900
"Recovery Spring"

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.650
Why not try it with
the entire E Class next time?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.900
So you want me in that party, too...

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.870
I'll think about it,
so just give me my clothes back.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.780
Yeah, there you go.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.120
Hey, no, wait!
I said I'd <i>think</i> about it, that's all!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:46.830
"Welcome, Red Devil!" "3-E's Rising Star"

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.460
Welcome to the E Class, Karma!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.250
I <i>said</i> I would <i>think</i> about it!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.920
What's with that mortifying banner?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.960
"Welcome, Red Devil!" "3-E's Rising Star"
"Karma joins the party!"

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.960
And why are you putting that in a dialog box?!

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:54.430
--And so we dragged Karma into our party,
--Hip-hip, hooray! Hip-hip, hooray!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.090
--getting one step closer
to defeating the Big Bad.
--Hip-hip, hooray! Hip-hip, hooray!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.970
--Look, I haven't made my mind up yet!
--Hip-hip, hooray! Hip-hip, hooray!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:10:02.120
"Next Time: The Seductive Witch"
